function heilungswegPage() {
  return shell(`
    ${pageHeader("heilungsweg")}
    <div style="max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1rem 3rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Charts &middot; Enneagram Homeopathy</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">The Human Path of Healing</h1>
      <p class="psycho-intro">This overview shows the path of healing according to the Enneagram-Homeopathy model by Detlef Rathmer: from the unconscious pattern through the realization of the passion to integration and healing.</p>
      <div class="psycho-img-wrap" style="margin:1.2rem 0 2.5rem;">
        <img src="../assets/schaubilder/heilungsweg/heilungsweg.jpg"
             alt="The Human Path of Healing According to Enneagram-Homeopathy"
             class="psycho-img" style="border-radius:12px;" />
      </div>

      <div class="vb-section" style="max-width:100%;">

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head"><span class="vb-typ__nr">Starting Point</span> The Essence</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">The path of healing does not begin with symptoms, with diagnoses, or with behavior. It begins with something that is often avoided in everyday medical practice because it cannot be measured: the essence of the human being. This does not mean an abstract ideal, but a concrete inner quality of being &ndash; a fundamental way in which a person is originally anchored in the world. This essence is not individual in the psychological sense, but archetypal. It manifests in nine basic forms, nine avenues to reality, nine ways of embodying love. This essence is not lost. It becomes obscured.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head"><span class="vb-typ__nr">The Overlay</span> Formation of the Ego</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">The moment a child experiences that their being is not unconditionally enough, a shift begins. Inner experience separates from outer life. Instead of acting out of being, the person begins to regulate themselves through adaptation, achievement, withdrawal, control, or merging. This is not a moral failure, but a neurobiologically and developmentally plausible protective mechanism. The Enneagram describes this process precisely, without judgment.</p>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">What emerges from this is the ego &ndash; not as a narcissistic caricature, but as a functional construct. It organizes perception, motivation, and action along a central experience of lack. Every Enneagram structure seeks something on the outside that was seemingly lost on the inside: order, recognition, identity, knowledge, security, freedom, power, or peace. This search is doomed to fail from the start because it takes place in the wrong place.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head"><span class="vb-typ__nr">The Passions</span> Fixations of the Nervous System</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">From this misorientation arise the typical passions. The term is often misunderstood. It is not about emotions in the narrow sense, but about chronic inner states of tension, fixations of the nervous system. Anger, pride, envy, fear, or sloth are not character flaws, but energetic ongoing patterns. They drive us, narrow perception, and keep the system stable &ndash; as long as the original essence is not accessible again. In clinical reality, we encounter them as symptoms, conflicts, exhaustion, or psychosomatic dynamics.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head"><span class="vb-typ__nr">The Homeopathic Approach</span> Resonance Instead of Symptom Treatment</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">Homeopathy has always worked primarily with resonance rather than against symptoms. It addresses what is alive in a human being, not pathology as an isolated object. Enneagram Homeopathy combines this perspective with a differentiated typology of consciousness. The remedy does not work against anger or fear, but upon the energetic balance between instinct, passion, and essence.</p>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">Particularly relevant here are the instinctual variants. Self-preservation, social, and sexual (one-to-one) instincts are not additional traits, but the energetic carriers of the passions. They determine where a person sets their focus, where they overcompensate, and where they are most vulnerable. Two people with the same Enneagram type can appear clinically completely different because their instinctual structure is different.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-typ">
          <h3 class="vb-typ__head"><span class="vb-typ__nr">What Healing Means</span> Returning Leadership</h3>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">Healing in this model does not mean destroying the ego or suppressing passions. That would be naive and therapeutically counterproductive. Healing means gradually returning leadership &ndash; away from reflex reactivity toward an inner presence that opens up choices again. The so-called Holy Ideas are not metaphysical concepts, but corrective modes of perception. They show how reality can be experienced beyond egoic distortion. Not as a goal, but as a reminder.</p>
          <p class="vb-typ__text">The path there is not a linear development plan or a spiritual success story. It is fragile, often uncomfortable, and confronting. It takes the person seriously without coddling them. Whoever lets go of cherished self-images, loses certainties, and no longer justifies their own suffering opens themselves up to a transformation that comes from within.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.6rem;margin-top:1rem;">
          <p class="vb-intro">Enneagram-Homeopathy understands disease as an expression of an inner alienation &ndash; not in a romantic sense, but as a real, tangible split between essence and life. The remedy does not support adaptation to a dysfunctional balance, but rather promotes a reorganization from within. When this succeeds, symptoms often change as a byproduct. Not because they were fought, but because they have lost their purpose.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-left:3px solid var(--gold);padding:.9rem 1.1rem;margin:1.8rem 0;background:var(--paper);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:.92rem;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.8;font-style:italic;">This is not a quick path. And it is not for everyone. But it is consistent. And it is honest.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
      ${relatedLinks([
        {route:"leidenschaft-und-wunde", label:"Passion & Wound"},
        {route:"wunden", label:"Wounds & Protective Strategies"},
        {route:"bewusstseinsuebungen", label:"Consciousness Exercises"},
      ])}
    </div>
  `);
}

